# GTKWave-Compatible SPICE Waveformat
# ------------------------------------
# This file demonstrates the format GTKWave accepts:
#   TIME,VALUE1,VALUE2,...
# 
# To read this in GTKWave:
#   1. Save the content to a .dat file
#   2. Run in GTKWave: GTKWave /path/to/output.dat
#   3. Signals can be selected via the Channel dropdown
#
# Generating with NGSPICE:
#   ngspice -b mycircuit.spice
#   # NGSPICE writes: time,value1,value2... in .control block
#   #   meas tran v1 MAX v(node1) from=start to=stop
#   #   meas tran v2 MAX v(node2) from=start to=stop
#   #   These points are output as: time1,val1_t1,val1_t2,...
#
# The .wrdata command saves a fixed-point format:
#   wrdata simu/tb_tx_T4_ST.dat v(pad) v(vin)
# This gives: sim_time, sig1_val, sig2_val, ...
# which GTKWave parses as floating point.

Format example:

    # Input: ngspice -b circuit.spice output.dat
    # Output in dat format:
    0.000000e-09, 1.200000, 0.000000, ...
    1.818182e-07, 0.150000, 0.050000, ...
